:S2_12 a dm:StoryCase ;
    dm:storyId "S2-12" ;
    dm:storySection "2.2.2" ;
    dm:storyKind "example" ;
    dm:pageSays "Giving a fifth of a stock block to charity and selling the rest cuts the gain and leaves more after tax than a full sale." ;
    dm:citesAuthority "Reg. 20.2031-2(b)(1) (high/low mean, by analogy); 170(e)(1)" ;
    dm:pageOutcome dm:Allow ;
    dm:storyScope dm:OutsideModel ;
    dm:outsideCategory dm:OutrightGiftToPublicCharity ;
    dm:outsideReason "partial stock gift with a sale" ;
    dm:pageAccuracyNote "The notes say the page assumes a 15 percent gain rate, ignoring the 20 percent rate and the 3.8 percent net investment income tax, and never shows whether the goal was met." .

:S2_13 a dm:StoryCase ;
    dm:storyId "S2-13" ;
    dm:storySection "2.3.2" ;
    dm:storyKind "example" ;
    dm:pageSays "A land gift paired with a life insurance trust that replaces it for heirs gives several tax benefits, if the policy is issued to the trust before the gift." ;
    dm:citesAuthority "2042(2); 2503(b); 2041(b)(2); Crummey (9th Cir. 1968); Cristofani (97 T.C. 74, 1991)" ;
    dm:pageOutcome dm:Allow ;
    dm:storyScope dm:OutsideModel ;
    dm:outsideCategory dm:LifeInsurance ;
    dm:outsideReason "wealth replacement insurance trust" ;
    dm:pageAccuracyNote "The notes say the page promises four tax benefits but names only about three." .

:S2_14 a dm:StoryCase ;
    dm:storyId "S2-14" ;
    dm:storySection "2.3.2" ;
    dm:storyKind "court case" ;
    dm:pageSays "Withdrawal rights make trust contributions present interests for the annual exclusion, and contingent beneficiaries may hold them too, multiplying the exclusions." ;
    dm:citesAuthority "Crummey (9th Cir. 1968); Cristofani (97 T.C. 74, 1991); 2503(b)" ;
    dm:pageOutcome dm:Allow ;
    dm:storyScope dm:OutsideModel ;
    dm:outsideCategory dm:TransferTaxArithmetic ;
    dm:outsideReason "annual exclusion and withdrawal powers" .

:S2_15 a dm:StoryCase ;
    dm:storyId "S2-15" ;
    dm:storySection "2.4.2" ;
    dm:storyKind "private letter ruling" ;
    dm:pageSays "A gift of a quarter undivided interest in art, held by the museum three months a year, was deductible generally at fair value." ;
    dm:citesAuthority "PLR 9303007; Reg. 1.170A-5(a)(2); 170(o)" ;
    dm:pageOutcome dm:Allow ;
    dm:storyScope dm:OutsideModel ;
    dm:outsideCategory dm:VehicleNotYetModeled ;
    dm:outsideReason "fractional interest in art" ;
    dm:pageAccuracyNote "The notes say the ruling predates the 2006 rules in 170(o): lesser-of valuation, completion within 10 years or at death, and recapture with a 10 percent penalty." .
